Darius Rucker is opening up about living  under the shadow of systemic racism in  the US for his entire life the country  singer spoke candidly with today's Harry  Smith but how the death of George Floyd  is how the reinvigorated black lives  matter movement has influenced change in  his own life especially after having  three children watch what kids go do  this I think they just have that age not  where they have to look at it  I've lived with racism my whole life  made me really sit there go I just can't  keep living my life like everything's  okay because everything's not okay  Darius admits that he's already had  conversations about how to act around  police with his three kids and recalls  his only experience being pulled over  driving a nice car getting stopped you  know knowing you're not speeding or  anything she could stop of course when  they recognized me everything's cool you  know why they get stopped officer oh you  know you know it was it wasn't speeding  I know I wasn't doing that I get stopped  because I was a you know like kind of  expensive car okay but it's happened a  million times it's just so not right  it's not and the thing is it's not gonna  change until enough people say it's  wrong the hootie and the blowfish  frontman added that as a black artist  and a predominantly white music genre he  came to accept racism as a simple fact  of life and recalled being told during  radio station visits that his music  wouldn't be played because he's black  really you get the pony oh that's just  you know that's just how it is you know  when I was going to radio stations and  you got guys telling me we're not gonna  play you cuz you're a black guy okay  that's just the way it is but I can't  live like that anymore I can't just go  it's okay and go on my life and you know  let somebody say something I know she  they shouldn't say now the singer is  sensing some sort of change  like anything he's ever experienced  before so much of the country really  wants some kind of change don't know  what we're gonna do don't know how we're  gonna do it but they want some kind of  changing so for me it feels different  the help I'm right  last month in the days following the  death of George Floyd the country singer  posted a lengthy letter to social media  platforms where he shared that Floyd's  death breaks me down to my core and  promised that he would no longer  perpetuate the myth that things are okay  now just a few days after the country  singer appeared on today he took to  social media to break the news that he  and his wife Beth Leonard have decided  to part ways  the singer announced the divorce along  with a photo of himself and Beth at the  CMA Awards in 2017 writing Beth and I  would like to share that after much  reflection we have made the decision to  consciously uncouple we remain close  friends and parenting partners and  continue to be each other's biggest  cheerleaders our priority will always be  our beautiful family we have so much  love in our hearts for each other and  will continue to encourage growth and  expansion in one another please be kind  as we take on this journey and we thank  you for your love and support always the  couple tied the knot in 2000 and share  two kids 19 year old daughter Daniela  and 15 year old son Jack Darius's third  child 25 year old Carolyn is from a  previous relationship
 

